WEBVTT

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:04.150
But it is not a virtual realit.

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:08.680
It is a planet that exists in the same 
place as Earth in a parallel wor.

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:15.210
<i>So the people in this 
world aren't virtual...</i>

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:19.070
<i>They're Earthlings that just 
exist in a parallel reality?</i>

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:32.420
<i>I... killed a man...</i>

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:45.990
Seriously?

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:49.730
<b>Play Games</b>

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:49.730
<b>Camera</b>

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:49.730
<b>WonSta</b>

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:56.160
<i>Did I really... kill a person?</i>

00:00:57.990 --> 00:00:59.080
<i>Shit...</i>

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:06.470
<i>I hate people.</i>

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:15.970
<i>I always wished they'd all just die...</i>

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:20.450
<i>But after killing just one,</i>

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:23.590
<i>my heart won't stop pounding.</i>

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:29.980
<i>Like a roller coaster... 
no, maybe more like skydiving...</i>

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:41.880
<i>There's no turning back.</i>

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:47.360
<i>I didn't even have any intention 
of starting now...</i>

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:57.750
<i>I'm falling.</i>

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:39.990
<b><b>A Murderer's<b> Summer</b></b></b>

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:47.240
Hey, pass it!

00:03:49.490 --> 00:03:50.640
Hey!

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:53.160
Who even gave him the ball?

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:54.830
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:01.610
Wow...

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:01.610
Here!

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:04.770
I know. Was he always that 
good at sports and stuff?

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:02.850
There!

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:04.900
There!

00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:07.390
Oops, sorry!

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:12.720
No worries.

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:19.140
It's amazing enough that you don't 
have to just watch anymore.

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:22.560
I guess I've gained a little more stamina.

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:26.350
I feel a little lighter 
than I did before, too.

00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:29.380
Maybe all that leveling up 
in the other world helped?

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:30.230
Maybe.

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:31.460
Here!

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:33.790
It's not as if I actually 
got over my illness.

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:33.550
Here!

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:36.450
Running in this world still wears me out.

00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:35.800
Here!

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:40.490
Man, I wish I'd felt like 
this before my tournament.

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:38.050
Here!

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:46.000
Does Yotsuya-kun know all 
that stuff about statuses?

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:49.460
I haven't talked to him since then.

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:51.940
I just... can't bring myself to.

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:53.000
Yeah...

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:03.120
Yuka-san? Yuka-san!

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:04.140
Huh?

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:06.360
What's up with Yotsuya-kun?

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:07.850
Huh? Oh...

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:10.900
I guess we didn't tell you 
everything that happened

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:13.120
when we saved the Arteros followers.

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:20.650
He... killed a man.

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:27.090
<b>And then?</b>

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:27.090
<b>Read</b>

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:27.090
<b>Yukarion</b>

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:27.090
<b>And then he lit the fire...
and burned him alive</b>

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:28.090
<b>Yukarion</b>

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:28.090
<b>And then he lit the fire...
and burned him alive</b>

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:28.090
<b>Are you serious?</b>

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:28.090
<b>Read</b>

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:31.600
<b>Are you serious?</b>

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:31.600
<b>Read</b>

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:31.600
<b>Yukarion</b>

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:31.600
<b>I saw it with my own eyes,
and honestly, it freaked me out</b>

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:32.880
Hey, Yotsuya!

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.390
You need to pass it around more.

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:41.490
Why's he so full of himself 
all of a sudden?

00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:46.500
<i>Yeah... it's gotta be hard on him.</i>

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:53.790
For real?

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:55.160
Yeah, for real!

00:05:59.930 --> 00:06:03.150
<i>I mean... I was the only 
one who killed anybody.</i>

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:08.550
<i>Who are you?</i>

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:18.310
<i>Who are you?</i>

00:06:21.790 --> 00:06:24.140
No, I know that's what it was!

00:06:24.140 --> 00:06:26.810
It was not. C'mon, give it a rest.

00:06:27.890 --> 00:06:29.860
I told you, it wasn't like that!

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:31.880
<i>I hate this city.</i>

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:31.150
Did you?

00:06:31.150 --> 00:06:32.690
Yes, I did!

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:39.290
<b>New Mail</b>

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:39.290
<b>Game Master</b>

00:06:37.550 --> 00:06:38.870
Game Master?

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:42.450
A mission? Wait, it's just me again?

00:06:47.060 --> 00:06:50.350
Well, it's not like I can 
run away from this now.

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:51.760
<b>New Mail</b>

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:51.760
<b>Game Master</b>

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:59.560
<b>Now that you've killed someone,
what are your honest feelings?</b>

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:11.910
What the hell was that?!

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:19.400
Was my killing someone 
part of the design, too?

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:23.040
But I mean... that was...

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:25.770
without a doubt...

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:31.460
my own decision.

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:36.400
Because I believed it was 
virtual... I was convinced...

00:07:37.230 --> 00:07:37.890
Damn it!

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:54.330
Hi.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:55.840
Who are you?!

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:57.150
You know...

00:07:57.650 --> 00:07:59.700
You should reply to my email.

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:02.120
Huh? Email? Reply?

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:03.790
<b>New Mail</b>

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:03.790
<b>Game Master</b>

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:05.370
Wait, are you...

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:08.860
The Master?! Or someone 
else from the future?!

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:12.060
Which is it?

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:15.470
You do not have the right to ask a ques.

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:17.100
I knew it! You <i>are</i> the Master!

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:20.680
And you're just... 
talking to me like it's normal.

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:25.940
So... uh...

00:08:26.620 --> 00:08:33.190
I half thought of them as being included 
among the people I wished would die.

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:36.770
They were...

00:08:37.150 --> 00:08:41.280
planning to kill some innocent religious 
people just to set an example.

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:46.570
On top of that, they tricked 
us and tried to kill us.

00:08:47.870 --> 00:08:50.710
To me, that makes them undeniably evil.

00:08:52.030 --> 00:08:54.760
But... the other half is different.

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:59.190
They believed what they 
were doing was right.

00:09:00.010 --> 00:09:00.700
So—

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:01.420
And?

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:03.760
Huh?

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:06.220
Answer my question.

00:09:09.870 --> 00:09:12.840
I feel like killing him was a mistake.

00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:15.150
If I'd known the truth, I wouldn't 
have wanted to do it.

00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:17.290
Okay. I'm done.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:19.510
That's it?

00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:25.200
That's it. I have nothing more to say.

00:09:26.970 --> 00:09:28.120
I see.

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:32.050
Then why don't I tell you 
about the next new player?

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:34.460
Really?

00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:38.620
Just like last time, 
there's someone I want you to meet.

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:43.300
Speaking of, what was up with that 
order to hit on Tokitate-san, anyway?

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:46.210
You do not have the right to ask a ques.

00:09:46.210 --> 00:09:48.940
Remember what I told you then? 
It meant what it said.

00:09:49.180 --> 00:09:51.230
Wait, what did it say again?

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:54.100
To save her from the restroom 
so I could hit on her...

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:56.890
And, uh... I forget.

00:09:56.890 --> 00:09:59.790
So, will you meet this player or not?

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:01.760
Well, sure, I will.

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:05.700
Shall we go, then?

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:09.190
A hat? What's that for?

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:14.960
m 0 0 l 260 0 l 260 180 l 0 180

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:14.960
[Breakdown of the Job Roulette]

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:14.960
►Warrior (Sword)  20%
►Warrior (Spear)  12.5% 
►Warrior (Ax)  12.5% 
►Wizard (Heat)  12.5% 
►Wizard (Wind)  12.5% 
►Wizard (Creature)  12.5% 
►Thief  7.5% 
►Hunter  7.5% 
►5 other random jobs  0.5% each

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:14.960
<b>Job
Roulette</b>

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:21.510
Hey, it's about time.

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:23.080
Get ready.

00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:31.100
The juice inside is very hot. 
Please be careful.

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:36.520
Well? What's the deal with 
this Chinese restaurant?

00:10:36.520 --> 00:10:39.480
The man sitting at the 
far end of the counter.

00:10:41.270 --> 00:10:44.290
Until just recently, he was a drug dealer.

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:45.610
Huh?!

00:10:45.890 --> 00:10:51.160
In 20 seconds, the new player is to 
enter this restaurant and kill him.

00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:54.670
A certain man has tricked him into 
thinking he won't be caught.

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:57.230
In 20 seconds?! The... 
The one doing the killing?!

00:10:57.230 --> 00:10:58.630
Ten. Nine.

00:10:58.630 --> 00:10:59.830
W-Wait a minute!

00:10:59.830 --> 00:11:03.860
The player's name is Torii Keita. 
Age 19, male.

00:11:03.860 --> 00:11:07.780
His brother Shuuji, age 14, 
is also involved in this plot.

00:11:07.780 --> 00:11:09.970
<i>Wait, 14? He's my age!</i>

00:11:09.970 --> 00:11:11.940
Three, two...

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:17.050
There he is! Over there!

00:11:17.290 --> 00:11:19.190
Die!

00:11:19.190 --> 00:11:21.110
Wait, which one is he?!

00:11:27.970 --> 00:11:29.940
Wh-What the hell's your problem?!

00:11:29.940 --> 00:11:32.950
Y-You really shouldn't kill people.

00:11:32.950 --> 00:11:34.030
Huh?

00:11:34.030 --> 00:11:36.870
I'm not sure what's going on, 
but you've been fooled into—

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:37.810
Shut your mouth, you bastard!

00:11:37.810 --> 00:11:38.890
Ow!

00:11:38.890 --> 00:11:40.460
That hurt...

00:11:40.790 --> 00:11:41.830
Hey!

00:11:46.730 --> 00:11:48.150
<i>Yeah...</i>

00:11:49.380 --> 00:11:51.980
<i>Idiots who don't understand what I'm saying</i>

00:11:52.380 --> 00:11:53.810
<i>really piss me off!</i>

00:11:54.130 --> 00:11:55.430
Ow, hot!

00:11:55.430 --> 00:11:56.090
Damn!

00:11:56.090 --> 00:12:00.050
<i>Of course, they only got tricked into 
coming here because they're idiots.</i>

00:12:04.270 --> 00:12:05.540
Shuuji!

00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:07.210
You son of a bitch!

00:12:07.210 --> 00:12:10.080
<i>Wasn't Shuuji the younger brother's name?</i>

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:11.530
<i>So this one must be...</i>

00:12:19.790 --> 00:12:21.960
Your target already ran away.

00:12:21.960 --> 00:12:24.490
Take your brother and run 
before the police show up.

00:12:24.490 --> 00:12:25.380
Move!

00:12:25.380 --> 00:12:26.760
<i>I have to kill him!</i>

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:28.660
What the hell?! Out of my way!

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:31.920
He's a yakuza drug dealer! 
Who cares if he dies?!

00:12:31.920 --> 00:12:33.510
Why are you protecting him?!

00:12:33.510 --> 00:12:35.100
It doesn't matter who he is!

00:12:35.340 --> 00:12:36.540
I won't let you kill him!

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:39.730
<b>Chinese Restaurant</b>

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:39.740
What is it?

00:12:40.270 --> 00:12:41.680
What's going on?

00:12:41.680 --> 00:12:43.180
I-I don't know!

00:12:43.180 --> 00:12:45.610
Some kid... looks like he'd 
be in middle school...

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:47.610
A kid?

00:12:47.610 --> 00:12:48.740
Stay out of my way!

00:12:49.220 --> 00:12:50.670
I'm not gonna let you!

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:01.790
Move.

00:13:03.610 --> 00:13:06.720
Do you work for the Koudangumi?

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:09.650
No, I don't.

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:12.760
Don't lie to me, you little brat!

00:13:16.030 --> 00:13:18.010
Hey, Yuu-kun...

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:30.050
<i>A child?</i>

00:13:33.430 --> 00:13:34.780
Wanna use this?

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:36.400
<i>A glove?</i>

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:41.960
Hey, punk!

00:13:45.210 --> 00:13:46.920
Creature Magic!

00:13:47.940 --> 00:13:50.130
Stop!

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:13.540
Ow...

00:14:15.090 --> 00:14:17.340
Wh-What the hell...

00:14:20.010 --> 00:14:21.170
Finally, they're here!

00:14:21.580 --> 00:14:23.280
Damn it! The cops!

00:14:23.280 --> 00:14:24.250
Move it!

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:26.290
Take your brother and run!

00:14:26.290 --> 00:14:28.940
H-Hey... just who are—

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:36.530
You bastard!

00:14:36.900 --> 00:14:40.250
Who do you think has been keeping 
you alive all this time?!

00:14:40.250 --> 00:14:41.790
Shut up.

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:45.610
First you lose to a kid, then you 
try to shoot him in the back?

00:14:47.890 --> 00:14:50.530
You're done, man.

00:14:53.960 --> 00:14:55.770
Nii-chan, hurry!

00:14:56.610 --> 00:14:58.700
Oh... R-Right.

00:15:02.470 --> 00:15:05.460
<i>Where'd those guys go, anyway?</i>

00:15:07.730 --> 00:15:11.260
I've cleared the quest, right? 
So I'm going home—

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:13.270
Let's talk for a little while.

00:15:13.650 --> 00:15:14.420
Huh?

00:15:15.370 --> 00:15:18.730
You stopped a murder today.

00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:20.350
So?

00:15:21.210 --> 00:15:25.450
How did it feel when you killed that man?

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:28.740
I don't know.

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:33.580
But I think I do know 
now what I need to do.

00:15:34.190 --> 00:15:38.290
If those brothers get arrested, my chance of 
success in the next quest will drop, right?

00:15:40.740 --> 00:15:44.870
I finally remembered what you said 
to me before I saved Tokitate-san.

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:49.340
Your success or failure here will influence 
your chances in the next que.

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:54.480
It was Tokitate-san who ended up 
completing that last quest for us.

00:15:54.980 --> 00:15:58.640
That means our chances of success 
in that quest did go up

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:00.770
because I succeeded in 
hitting on her, right?

00:16:02.030 --> 00:16:05.690
The reason she held out until the 
end, despite her personality,

00:16:06.200 --> 00:16:09.280
is because those naked photos 
of her didn't get out,

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:12.920
meaning this world was still the 
reality she wanted to return to.

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:16.160
It's all strictly mental stuff,

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:19.030
but that definitely increased our 
chances of completing the quest.

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:22.360
And this time...

00:16:24.910 --> 00:16:31.360
I created a world he'd want to return to 
because he and his brother weren't arrested.

00:16:32.100 --> 00:16:35.000
And that increases my chances 
in the next quest.

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:36.220
Is that all?

00:16:36.580 --> 00:16:37.670
What do you mean?

00:16:38.620 --> 00:16:40.670
No comment on the value 
of his life or anything?

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:45.600
It has no value.

00:16:46.570 --> 00:16:49.780
Every single person who's dumb 
enough to be tricked into killing

00:16:49.780 --> 00:16:51.720
deserves to die.

00:16:55.250 --> 00:16:59.690
The truth is that all humans ought to die, 
starting with the least valuable ones.

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:03.750
That blond guy wouldn't be needed 
either, if he wasn't a player.

00:17:07.530 --> 00:17:09.160
That's hilarious!

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:13.830
I heard Nakata-kun asked out a 
girl in his tennis club, too!

00:17:13.830 --> 00:17:14.870
Another cop car?

00:17:15.230 --> 00:17:17.780
Yeah, I feel like we've 
heard a lot of them today.

00:17:17.780 --> 00:17:19.080
I wonder if something happened.

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:20.230
Maybe a murder?

00:17:20.230 --> 00:17:21.490
Whoa, scary...

00:17:21.490 --> 00:17:24.830
Hey, Iu, what if there was 
a murder? That's scary!

00:17:24.830 --> 00:17:26.460
Murder, huh?

00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:29.100
Yeah, that has to be rough...

00:17:29.300 --> 00:17:32.340
Rough? What the heck does that mean?

00:17:32.340 --> 00:17:34.770
Oh, sorry! Did I just say something?

00:17:34.770 --> 00:17:36.670
Uh, are you okay?

00:17:36.670 --> 00:17:39.700
<i>Today, we'll be bathing a hedgehog.</i>

00:17:38.040 --> 00:17:39.530
I'm home.

00:17:39.530 --> 00:17:40.920
Welcome back.

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:46.040
<i>What we'll need is our hedgehog, 
warm water, and a soft towel.</i>

00:17:40.920 --> 00:17:44.950
Apparently a guy with a gun was 
arrested near the station.

00:17:44.950 --> 00:17:46.300
Really?

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:51.160
<i>First, gently place the 
hedgehog in the warm water.</i>

00:17:48.110 --> 00:17:49.380
That doesn't scare you?

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:50.600
Sure it does.

00:17:51.160 --> 00:17:55.700
<i>With its whole body submerged, 
gently wipe off the dirt.</i>

00:17:53.330 --> 00:17:57.120
Well, I'm going to start on dinner. 
Could you clean the bathtub?

00:17:55.700 --> 00:18:00.020
<i>Be sure to avoid spraying it 
directly with the shower head.</i>

00:17:57.120 --> 00:17:58.970
Okay, sure.

00:18:00.530 --> 00:18:08.850
<i>Finally, wrap it up in a soft 
towel and gently dry it off.</i>

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:05.160
<i>She once got so scared that she cried</i>

00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:07.830
<i>just because there was a 
robber in the neighborhood...</i>

00:18:10.210 --> 00:18:13.300
I saved them to increase 
Shindou-san and Hakozaki-san's

00:18:13.300 --> 00:18:16.850
chances of survival, 
even if only by one percent.

00:18:17.230 --> 00:18:20.040
Hey! Did you forget about me?

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:20.990
OK

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:21.620
I didn't forget

00:18:20.450 --> 00:18:22.280
I remember, I remember

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:22.280
Who are you?

00:18:22.270 --> 00:18:24.810
Well, you haven't been 
coming around lately.

00:18:24.810 --> 00:18:28.030
Yeah, well, a lot of stuff happened,

00:18:28.030 --> 00:18:31.250
and I was starting to feel 
kinda mentally down...

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:33.640
Don't worry, though! I'm much better—

00:18:33.640 --> 00:18:37.750
Oh, hey! There were a bunch of 
police sirens in town today...

00:18:37.750 --> 00:18:39.350
Hey! I'm still talking!

00:18:39.350 --> 00:18:41.840
What do you think happened? 
Pretty freaky, right?

00:18:41.840 --> 00:18:45.510
Doesn't look like there's any info 
online about it yet, either.

00:18:43.140 --> 00:18:45.120
I'm gonna go get a drink.

00:18:45.530 --> 00:18:48.750
This is weird! Definitely weird!

00:18:48.750 --> 00:18:51.460
So what I thought at that moment

00:18:51.460 --> 00:18:55.100
was that there must be some 
scary secret hidden somewhere!

00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:59.590
I watched this video a couple days ago, 
and I realized there was a hint hidden in it!

00:18:59.590 --> 00:19:04.660
Basically, there are tiny antenna in my head, 
and when this incident happened—

00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:03.980
Anyway, I wonder when we'll 
be getting the next quest...

00:19:07.780 --> 00:19:10.320
The value of humans, huh?

00:19:11.520 --> 00:19:14.110
And you're deciding that as if you're

00:19:14.110 --> 00:19:17.840
some anonymous Internet user who's 
better than everyone else?

00:19:18.870 --> 00:19:21.710
Just who do you think you are?

00:19:25.570 --> 00:19:29.260
I'm no one. Just some kid.

00:19:30.010 --> 00:19:32.630
Just a dumb kid with delusions of grandeur.

00:19:33.500 --> 00:19:38.810
And I'm fully aware that I'm wrong.

00:19:39.500 --> 00:19:40.690
I admit it.

00:19:41.600 --> 00:19:43.760
I know that, honestly.

00:19:45.360 --> 00:19:49.770
But... How do I put it? 
The realization hasn't set in.

00:19:50.170 --> 00:19:53.890
Only I am right, and the rest 
of the world is wrong.

00:19:54.400 --> 00:19:56.230
That's how I feel.

00:19:56.230 --> 00:20:01.090
Of course, I know in my head that that's 
just proof of my delusions of grandeur.

00:20:02.190 --> 00:20:02.960
But...

00:20:05.230 --> 00:20:07.390
If that's true, then so what, right?

00:20:10.380 --> 00:20:11.880
I want to help everyone now...

00:20:11.880 --> 00:20:13.850
Like hell I'm gonna die!

00:20:13.850 --> 00:20:14.940
Please help me.

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:16.820
Thanks!

00:20:20.130 --> 00:20:21.560
Thanks for everything.

00:20:28.090 --> 00:20:29.660
Who are you?

00:20:32.300 --> 00:20:35.710
I fight only for the justice 
that I believe in.

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:39.380
I always have... and I always will!

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:51.930
Q: Where is your justice?

00:22:23.860 --> 00:22:25.400
<b>News Flash</b>

00:22:29.130 --> 00:22:31.090
<i>I hate that city.</i>

00:22:31.750 --> 00:22:35.030
<i>I hate everyone living in that city.</i>

00:22:36.120 --> 00:22:39.540
<b>Production of season 2 is confirmed!</b>

00:22:39.540 --> 00:22:41.880
<b>The next stage will be...</b>

00:22:42.130 --> 00:22:48.800
<b>Space.</b>

00:22:43.170 --> 00:22:47.800
Being in space is a million times more 
exciting than that shithole Tokyo!

00:22:48.800 --> 00:22:54.220
You will all give your hearts 
for the sake of humani.

00:22:54.720 --> 00:22:58.640
<b>The mysterious beauties</b>

00:22:56.680 --> 00:22:58.640
<b>Yaana (27)</b>

00:22:58.640 --> 00:23:00.690
